Read-only review under the 2026-09-05 brief. Adds one research note and no code.

Verdict: there is no genuine new energy opportunity on the live path. Energy is
already wired into every slot it could occupy (trust_energy engine selection,
goal_energy in plan_in_model, energy-fitness QD, action-effect prior, hazard
pruner, goal-energy guidance) and each measured neutral or null. The two measured
bottlenecks are generator decode (98 percent of wall clock, lookup-table engines)
and first-contact discovery by the tier-1 explorer (813 actions vs human 22 on
r11l level 0). RHAE squares the action ratio, so halving a blind search moves a
level from 0.07 to 0.29 points; only a correct model scores.

The note maps the bottlenecks with populations, inventories the live energy
slots, lists 14 rejected candidates with the artifact or rule that rejects each,
and explains why the one energy-shaped open door (a contrastive within-action-id
affordance objective) is still not proposed.

Two record-hygiene items recorded for file owners, not acted on here: the
S0-S4 structural-energy ban has no exclusion-manifest entry (prose only), and
GAP-ARCH-WORLD-MODEL-TRUST-ENERGY still reads status open after exp4811
answered it.

